          "id": "e2c0c5fcce2e57aad03d51ddc7ecd106033aeeec",
          "message": "test(core-term): close mutation gap in scroll-region damage tracking (2026-08-06 audit) (#982)\n\n## Summary\n\nScheduled test-quality-control pass, continuing\n`docs/bugs/2026-08-01-test-quality-audit-followup.md`. Full writeup:\n`docs/bugs/2026-08-06-test-quality-audit-followup.md`.\n\n- Static-audited everything changed since the last pass\n(`eb03ee9f..HEAD`, 4 commits — the `pixelflow-ir` → `pixelflow-codegen`\ncrate split) against `docs/STYLE.md`'s \"Test Public API\" rule: **no new\nviolations**. The crate split looked large in `git diff --stat`, but\nwith rename detection it was mostly file moves with import-path updates,\nnot new test logic.\n- Mutation-tested (`cargo-mutants`) the delta's only new production\nlogic: core-term's scrollback/cursor damage tracking\n(`last_snapshot_view`, `last_cursor_mark`, `scrollback_generation`).\nFound one real gap: `get_render_snapshot`'s `view_changed || grid_dirty`\n(`emulator/mod.rs:230`) survived being mutated to `&&`, because every\nexisting damage-tracking test's view-change trigger happened to also\ndirty the same rows through the normal per-line path.\n- Added `scroll_region_push_dirties_rows_outside_the_region`: uses a\npartial scroll region (`DECSTBM`) to decouple the two signals — rows\noutside the region are untouched by the scroll itself but must still\nredraw because the scrollback generation bumped. Confirmed via targeted\n`cargo-mutants` re-run: 0 missed (was 1).\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `cargo test -p core-term --lib` — 439/439 passing\n- [x] `cargo clippy -p core-term --lib --tests` — clean\n- [x] `cargo fmt -p core-term --check` — clean\n- [x] `cargo check --workspace` — clean\n- [x] `cargo mutants -p core-term --file\ncore-term/src/term/emulator/mod.rs --re \"230:42\"` — 0 missed (was 1)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01QNus5Vp6DLnK6StKzgjb3a\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNus5Vp6DLnK6StKzgjb3a)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
